{%- comment -%}
  Not found. Port of app/not-found.tsx.

  THE COPY IS WRITTEN NOW, 2026-09-28. It was deliberately blank until then, on
  the reasoning that filler prose is worse than an honest placeholder on a page
  where the reader is already lost. That held while nothing else on the page
  could help them; it stopped holding once the catalogue was complete, because
  now there is somewhere specific to send them.

  WHAT A 404 HERE IS ACTUALLY FOR, and it shapes every line of the copy: the
  most likely reason a reader is on this page is a link to a piece that has been
  taken off the shop. 106 products were deleted in one go on 2026-09-13 and 20
  more went with the catalogue replacement, so old links to this store are real
  and there are a lot of them. The body says that plainly instead of blaming the
  reader's typing.

  TWO WAYS OUT, NOT ONE. The button is the catalogue, because this is a shop and
  the catalogue is where everything currently made is. The second is search,
  because a reader who arrived on a dead product link usually knows the name of
  the piece they wanted, and the catalogue makes them hunt for it. It is a plain
  link rather than a second button: two buttons of equal weight is a choice, and
  the shop is the answer for almost everyone.

  The copy is section settings rather than hardcoded, like everything else the
  brand says, so the studio can change it in the theme editor. Both routes are
  drawn only when their label is set, so blanking a label removes the control
  rather than leaving a dead one.

  THE BUTTON IS `snippets/button.liquid`. This section used to retype the
  primary button's class string, which is exactly what that snippet was
  extracted to stop.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign shop_href = routes.all_products_collection_url
  assign search_href = routes.search_url
-%}

<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-5 py-section text-center">
    <p class="text-micro uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink-subtle" data-numeric>404</p>

    <h1 class="font-display text-h1 leading-h1 text-ink">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
    </h1>

    <p class="wl-measure text-small text-ink-muted">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body, label: 'body', lines: 2 %}
    </p>

    {%- if section.settings.cta != blank -%}
      <div class="mt-2">
        {% render 'button', label: section.settings.cta, href: shop_href, variant: 'primary' %}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.search_label != blank -%}
      <a
        href="{{ search_href }}"
        class="text-caption text-ink-muted underline underline-offset-4 transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:text-brand"
      >{{ section.settings.search_label }}</a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "404",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The page a reader lands on when a link is dead. The most likely cause is a link to a piece that is no longer in the shop, so the body says so rather than suggesting the reader mistyped. Blank a label and that control is not drawn at all." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "We cannot find that page" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body", "default": "The link may be out of date, or the piece it pointed to may no longer be in the shop. Everything we currently make is one tap away." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta", "label": "Button", "default": "Browse the shop" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "search_label", "label": "Secondary link", "default": "Or search for a piece by name", "info": "Goes to the search page. A reader who arrived on a dead product link usually knows the name of the piece they wanted." }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
